2375-## D173 · 2026-10-25 · Isolated provider smoke before a larger concurrency test
2376-
2377-- Alex approved proceeding with a small test and required preserving the working database: “don't contaminate the current working db ... check the batch API usage correctly ... small scale test before moving forward”. All existing databases remain read-only; no merge or production activation is authorized.
2378-- The [registered smoke](research/2026-10-25-api-smoke/plan.md) repeats two unchanged extraction requests and two unchanged Jev requests, with three fresh samples of two serial controls and one two-worker arm. Maximum 36 requests; conservative $1.50 reservation ceiling; no automatic retries. This is ordinary API concurrency, not OpenAI's asynchronous Batch API, and is not end-to-end or 10x acceptance.
2379-- The isolated transport reserves money before dispatch, retains unknown usage after failures, and closes admission on any worker failure or cancellation. A synchronized dispatch decision separates work not yet committed to sending from in-flight work. The provider endpoints, pinned models, response shapes and price envelopes were checked against the official documentation. Existing prompts, product behavior, golds and default transports remain unchanged.
2380-- Result: [36-request smoke](../poc/reports/2026-10-25-api-smoke/results.md) completed with valid responses, no retries, and all 122 pre-existing database files unchanged. Median two-request speed ratios were 1.08x extraction and 1.77x Jev. Fresh extraction varied between controls; one of 27 Jev categorical comparisons differed. This passes API integration, not semantic or 10x acceptance. A small end-to-end comparison remains next; no production promotion.
