2389-## D175 · 2026-10-25 · Publish sequential cleanup separately from experiments
2390-
2391-- Alex asked to commit and push fixes/cleanup that relate to the current sequential version. The pure request-construction cleanup was isolated in a separate worktree and pushed as `07aaff0` on `cleanup/sequential-requests`. It centralizes existing request and hash construction without changing payloads or processing behavior; all 3,595 archived request identities and 123 sequential product/corpus tests pass.
2392-- The branch contains no concurrent runner, parallel matching, experimental transport or project-eligibility change. It is pushed, not merged into `main`. Experimental work remains local in the original worktree.
