2400:## D177 · 2026-10-25 · Modify and test NAVER admission on one frozen context
2401-
2402-- Alex explicitly asked: “那你改了然后验证这一条啊”. The [NAVER-only test](research/2026-10-25-naver-admission/plan.md) changes the experimental T6 role to v11, retains the same category text, schema, model, horizon check, matching and writer, and compares three fresh controls with three fresh treatments. The original v23 configuration remains the default.
2403-- The treatment removes mandatory numeric-card instructions, asks first for a material uncovered business question, and distinguishes an announced milestone's quantitative completion criterion from an annual forecast. It names no NAVER-specific facts. The system message shrinks by 172 characters; non-system request content is identical.
2404-- Six isolated single-item rounds use the exact pre-NAVER state from the failed serial control, with a new $0.60/36-call ceiling and no network retries. Their scope ends after matching/writing; daily judging and wider extraction quality are not tested. The existing working databases remain read-only. No schema or general horizon-policy change is authorized by this experiment.
2405-
2406-- Result: [six fresh samples](../poc/reports/2026-10-25-naver-admission/results.md) retained appropriate project coverage in 3/3 treatments versus 2/3 controls. The other control attached platform-use evidence to Rubin production instead; the two passing controls also proposed discarded annual-capacity questions. Treatment preserved plan attribution and the 200 MW / 2028 milestone without that extra question. Twelve physical requests used $0.009831 at Standard list prices and $0.031480 conservative accounting; all 124 protected databases were unchanged. This supports the candidate on this source only; the default remains v23, with no schema or horizon-policy change.
2407-- Publication: the versioned prompt, T6-only test configuration and measured outputs are pushed on `fix/thesis-admission-v11` as `884866055cc265455bb72d25cd22e71db10e6558`, based on the sequential cleanup. The paid experiment harness and concurrency runtime remain isolated in the original worktree; no merge or default activation.
