     1	# Hivemind rebuild: working instructions
     2	
     3	This repository, `hivemind`, rebuilds Hivemind from the old repository `../tn-hivemind`, one piece at a time. The rules below are that repository's
     4	principles and 54 lessons, merged and cut down to the practices that hold whatever the new code's structure turns out
     5	to be. Rules that assumed the old architecture are left out; an architectural rule enters this file only once the new
     6	design has decided it. The incidents behind these rules are history in `../tn-hivemind/docs/LESSONS.md`: read it for
     7	the reason behind a rule, never as a rule.
     8	
     9	## How these rules work
    10	
    11	The old repository added one lesson per incident, and the same failures repeated, because a lesson was a sentence read
    12	once and applied fix by fix; none sat at the decision to act. Here each rule sits at the decision it governs (diagnose,
    13	design, code, test, verify) and, where it can, names what must be written down before that decision is taken. A rule
    14	that code can enforce becomes a check, and this file names the check. A new lesson amends the rule at its decision; it
    15	becomes a new rule only when no rule covers that decision.
    16	
    17	## Authority and scope
    18	
    19	- Alex's messages win, then recorded decisions (`docs/DECISIONS.md`), then the governing design documents. Build what
